<article class="env-lemma" id="0B2G">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0B2G">Lemma <span data-tag="0B2G">33.16.8</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of schemes locally of finite type over a base scheme $S$. Let $x \in X$ be a point. Set $y = f(x)$ and assume that $\kappa (y) = \kappa (x)$. Then the following are equivalent </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$\text{d}f : T_{X/S, x} \longrightarrow T_{Y/S, y}$ is injective, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$f$ is unramified at $x$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The morphism $f$ is locally of finite type by Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/01T8" data-tag="01T8">29.15.8</a>. The map $\text{d}f$ is injective, if and only if $\Omega _{Y/S, y} \otimes \kappa (y) \to \Omega _{X/S, x} \otimes \kappa (x)$ is surjective (Lemma <a href="/tag/0B2F" data-tag="0B2F">33.16.6</a>). The exact sequence $f^*\Omega _{Y/S} \to \Omega _{X/S} \to \Omega _{X/Y} \to 0$ (Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/01UX" data-tag="01UX">29.33.9</a>) then shows that this happens if and only if $\Omega _{X/Y, x} \otimes \kappa (x) = 0$. Hence the result follows from Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/02GF" data-tag="02GF">29.36.14</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>